I think that the fundamental problem is that we load the markdown 2 times.&#x20;

TextEditorPane reloads every time when a document is made active. i think this is the trigger that causes the double load.

when we open a file, the first tab 'definition' is shown, but it seems the markdown context data of the prompt already gets loaded in some effect. There i can see the correct prompt in some of the breakpoints.

Then, we switch tab to 'prompt' and the flush gets called again. but now the value for markdown is '' (empty string).&#x20;

We did originally designed the components in such a way that they did not have to be reloaded all the time cause it is slow. so the editor remained loaded in memory and through service and events, one or the other editor becomes visible. this seems to have been broken. I think this is why we are loosing the text.

